 # Real-time Voxel Editing with Section Rebuild
 
-Also called: Incremental Section Mesh Update, Section Rebuild
+Also called: Incremental Section Mesh Update, Live Voxel Editing & Re-meshing, Section Rebuild
 
 ## Overview
-This method enables immediate visual feedback for voxel placement and removal by regenerating mesh geometry only for the affected 16x16x16 section and any adjacent sections if the edit occurs on a section boundary [S1, unofficial]. It solves the latency issue of full-chunk regeneration by limiting updates to the immediate neighborhood of a block change, ensuring real-time responsiveness during voxel editing [S1, unofficial]. Unlike full rebuilds, it relies on boundary detection to determine which neighboring sections require recalculation [S1, unofficial].
+This method enables immediate visual feedback for voxel placement and removal by regenerating mesh geometry only for the affected 16×16×16 section and any adjacent sections if the edit occurs on a section boundary [S1, unofficial]. It solves the latency issue of full-chunk regeneration by limiting updates to the immediate neighborhood of a block change, ensuring real-time responsiveness during voxel editing [S1, unofficial]. Unlike full rebuilds, it relies on boundary detection to determine which neighboring sections require recalculation [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** The 3D coordinates $(i, j, k)$ of the modified voxel within the chunk, the new `BlockType` (e.g., AIR, STONE), and the chunk's internal voxel array `mBlocks`.
-*   **Output:** Updated vertex and index buffers for the affected mesh sections, uploaded to the GPU.
+*   **Input:** The 3D coordinates $(i, j, k)$ of the modified voxel within the chunk, the new `BlockType` (e.g., AIR, STONE), and the chunk's internal voxel array `mBlocks` [S1, unofficial].
